  "query_preview": "/THURSDAY THROUGH TUESDAY/...\nIssued at 318 AM CDT Wed Aug 26 2026\n\n(Thursday - Friday Night)\n\nDry weather with low humidity and near to slightly below normal \ntemperatures are forecast to end the work week thanks to a ridge of \nhigh pressure moving into the mid-Mississippi Valley. Highs each day \nare expected to be in the mid 80s, with lows in the upper 50s to mid \n60s. \n\n\n(Saturday - Tuesday)\n\nEnsemble guidance is in good agreement that the mid/upper level \nridge will shift back eastward by late this weekend. This portends \nto a return to summertime heat beginning Sunday. Dewpoint (humidity) \nlevels though look slower to increase, and likely will stay \nrelatively low until Tuesday. This is when dewpoints may pool closer \nto a cold front that may get hung up just to our north. Heat index \nvalues are more likely to approach or exceed the century mark by \nTuesday. All in all, this looks like a fairly typical late August \nheat where dewpoints (relative humidity) levels are quite a bit \nlower than early to mid summer levels.",
